	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Browse recent Lark/Feishu docs and search all docs.

  ld [query]   recent docs; 2+ chars also searches all of Lark

↩ open · ⌘↩ copy link · ⌥↩ copy title + link

When the session has expired, `ld` shows a 'Sign in to Lark' row — ↩ on it
opens Chrome to refresh the cookie jar. There is no separate login keyword;
the row appears exactly when it is needed. (It fires the `login` External
Trigger, reachable as alfred://runtrigger/com.lukew.larkdocs/login/ .)

Source of truth: ~/.dotfiles/config/AlfredApp/lark-docs (this directory is a
symlink into it). Needs Homebrew node and Google Chrome.</string>
